# f1 = fill, f2 = fillLowest
# This is how a compiler of classes writes a constructor for engines without classes: the base is a captured variable, and what the base returned stands for `this` where it is an object.
# The whole body of Animal is two stores and it returns undefined, so `_this` is `this`. The whole body of Dog returns `_this`, so the `_this` of Puppy is `this` too.
# Behind the guards that say what a read of `call` off each base finds, every store is among the first things that happen to the new object, and the allocation lists them all.
# RUN(LOOK): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# LOOK: AreMembersUnchanged conditions=[{{*}}side=Static key="call"
# LOOK: = NewObject -, {{*}}fields=[0, 1, 2]
# RUN(LOWEST): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# LOWEST: AreMembersUnchanged conditions=[{{*}}side=Static key="call"{{*}}side=Static key="call"
# LOWEST: = NewObject -, {{*}}fields=[0, 1, 2, 3]
# RUN: run-in-shell globalThis.hits = 0; globalThis.change = () => { }; globalThis.report = () => globalThis.hits;
# CHECK: 115
# CHECK-NEXT: name,legs,age
# CHECK-NEXT: 120
# CHECK-NEXT: name,legs,age,toy
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# In the run OWNCALL a `call` of its own lies on Animal from turn five of the first loop on. It counts the keys that the object has when it arrives: none.
# RUN(OWNCALL): run-in-shell globalThis.hits = 0; globalThis.change = (animal) => { animal.call = function (self) { globalThis.hits += Object.keys(self).length + 1; self.name = "other"; self.legs = 1; }; }; globalThis.report = () => globalThis.hits;
# OWNCALL: 110
# OWNCALL-NEXT: name,legs,age
# OWNCALL-NEXT: 110
# OWNCALL-NEXT: name,legs,age,toy
# OWNCALL-NEXT: 15
# OWNCALL-NEXT: exited with 0
# In the run RETURNS the `call` of its own returns an object, which stands for `this` from there on: the construction gives it, and the object that was made is dropped.
# RUN(RETURNS): run-in-shell globalThis.hits = 0; globalThis.change = (animal) => { animal.call = function (self) { globalThis.hits += Object.keys(self).length + 1; return { legs: 2, name: "made" }; }; }; globalThis.report = () => globalThis.hits;
# RETURNS: 110
# RETURNS-NEXT: legs,name,age
# RETURNS-NEXT: 110
# RETURNS-NEXT: legs,name,age,toy
# RETURNS-NEXT: 15
# RETURNS-NEXT: exited with 0
# In the run SETTER an accessor lies under `age` above every Dog from turn five of the first loop on.
# RUN(SETTER): run-in-shell globalThis.hits = 0; globalThis.change = (animal) => { Object.defineProperty(animal.prototype, "age", { get() { return 10; }, set(value) { globalThis.hits++; }, configurable: true }); }; globalThis.report = () => globalThis.hits;
# SETTER: 130
# SETTER-NEXT: name,legs
# SETTER-NEXT: 210
# SETTER-NEXT: name,legs,toy
# SETTER-NEXT: 15
# SETTER-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(CHECKED): run-in-shell testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime globalThis.hits = 0; globalThis.change = (animal) => { animal.call = function (self) { globalThis.hits += Object.keys(self).length + 1; return { legs: 2, name: "made" }; }; }; globalThis.report = () => globalThis.hits;
